To optimize the code for extracting entities using DeepPavlov's NER model, consider the following streamlined approach:

```python
ner_preds = ner_model([text])
tokens, labels = ner_preds

entities = []
current_entity = {'type': None, 'text': '', 'start': None, 'end': None}

for i, (token, label) in enumerate(zip(tokens, labels)):
    if label != 'O':
        ent_type = label.split('-')[-1]

        if current_entity['type'] == ent_type:
            current_entity['text'] += token
        else:
            if current_entity['type']:
                entities.append(current_entity)
            current_entity = {'type': ent_type, 'text': token, 'start': i, 'end': i}
    else:
          if current_entity['text']: # to handle entity at the end of text
            entities.append(current_entity)
            current_entity = {'type': None, 'text': '', 'start': None, 'end': None}

entities.append(current_entity) if current_entity['text'] else None # in case last token is an entity

entities
```

This optimized code simplifies entity extraction, ensuring entities are correctly captured without introducing extra spaces and improving readability for easier comprehension.

